      "value": "@{628d00a6b624bb0b622328ef|full_name}: \nI was mostly referring to Settings / Options for Audio related things not being really consistent.\n# What do I mean with this?\nBasically, in the Audio Tab of the Quick Menu or Main Menu we have both a Volume Slider and a Mute / Toggle button for each audio option / setting. This is not the case in other parts of the Menu. (see Attachments below)\nMy biggest complaint here are the HUD Audio Settings, for the Notification sounds we only have a toggle / mute button but no volume slider. For the Mic Toggle Sound we only have a volume slider.\n# What would I like changed?\nConsider adding a volume slider to the Notification Sound and a separate `Play Mic Toggle Sound` toggle. This would make it more consistent with how other Audio Settings are done (e.g. Chatbox Notification Sound) and would allow users to separately change the Notification Sound volume, as well as Quickly turn the Mic Toggle Sound off.\nOh and btw, if we are already talking about Audio Settings / Volume Sliders, please consider adding one for the Loading Screen Music. I know a lot of people who have their entire UI Sounds turned off completely, because they want to listen to their own music and not the loading screen. (`Loading Screen Volume` in either the UI or Audio Category of the Main Menu Settings Tab)\nEdit: If you want to I can open up one canny for the Audio Settings (Mute Toggle Sound and the Notification Sound) and another one for the Loading Screen Volume Slider.\nEdit 2: This text got way longer than I planned it to be xD\n# Attachments:\nHere screenshots of different Audio Settings throughout the UI:",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
